**DNS Amplification, Explained:**

DNS amplification is a technique used to significantly improve the speed and efficiency of DNS resolution by utilizing multiple DNS servers to query for the same domain name-server. This approach allows users to bypass geographically distant servers, reducing latency and improving performance.

**Code for DNS Amplification:**

```python
import React, { useState, useEffect } from "react";
import dns from "dnsjs";

const DNS_SERVERS = [
  "dns14.example.com",
  "dns2.example.com",
  "dns3.example.com",
];
